    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192879": {
      "title": "Associate Dean",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Associate Dean Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: Barrett, The Honors College Location Downtown campus Open Date Sep 07, 2026 Description Barrett, The Honors College , is seeking an Associate Dean for Barrett on the ASU Downtown campus. The Associate Dean provides strategic leadership for the Downtown Barrett campus and is responsible for delivering a high-impact, high-value, and innovative honors experience for Downtown Barrett students in coordination with the Dean. The Associate Dean is also a key member of the Barrett leadership team, collaborating with the deans to shape and advance college-level initiatives and priorities as well as enhancing the framework for Barrett in multiple locations. We welcome applications from faculty currently serving at Arizona State University in an Honors Faculty Fellow position with the rank of Associate Teaching Professor or Teaching Professor. This role includes 0.5 FTE in administrative responsibilities , and the selected candidate is expected to maintain a 0.5 FTE faculty workload . Essential Functions: Provide leadership and support for the Barrett staff, faculty, and students at the Downtown campus, including direct supervision of at least one staff position; follow college-wide initiatives, processes, and practices to ensure a consistent high-quality Barrett experience across campuses. Assess honors student enrollment, retention, and success at the campus as well as the impact of the Barrett Downtown experience, and implement changes based on those assessments. Continue to articulate the identity of and priorities for Barrett Downtown, reflecting the specific needs and characteristics of that community while also aligning with the college mission and values. Oversee annual budget in line with strategic priorities of the college and the Barrett Downtown community. Coordinate with ASU and Barrett recruitment and admissions teams to continue to grow the Barrett Downtown community. Collaborate with Downtown colleges, leadership, and faculty to develop and refine course offerings, programs, support, and opportunities for Barrett Downtown students. Collaborate with external partners (businesses, state and local government, other institutions, etc.) to develop and continue professional development opportunities for Barrett Downtown students. Communicate with current and prospective students and their families about the Barrett Downtown experience. Work closely with the deans, faculty chair, and senior staff leaders; actively participate in the Barrett leadership team; and represent the college on committees and at events. Other duties as assigned Working Environment The Associate Dean works in a dynamic higher education environment that includes office, classroom, and campus-wide settings. The position requires regular interaction with faculty, staff, students, and community partners. Duties are performed in both individual and group settings, including meetings, presentations, and campus events. The Associate Dean must spend a minimum of 50% of their assigned work time physically present on the Downtown campus performing administrative, supervisory, and student-facing responsibilities. The role may also require presence at other locations as needed to support institutional initiatives and operations. Work is primarily performed in a standard office environment with extended periods of sitting, computer use, and participation in meetings. The position may require occasional evening and weekend work to support campus events, meetings, and special projects. Travel between campuses or to community sites may be required. Qualifications Required qualifications: Terminal degree in field of specialty and qualifications commensurate with a career-track associate teaching or teaching professor position Outstanding skills in communication and collaboration. Demonstrated commitment to advancing the values of the ASU Charter Must be a current Honors Faculty Fellow within Barrett, The Honors College at Arizona State University Desired qualifications: Higher education leadership experience Understanding of the Downtown campus and/or its academic disciplines Application Instructions To apply for this position, please include: A letter of application indicating relevant academic and professional experience CV A list of three professional references with contact information Emailed applications will not be accepted. The application deadline is Monday, September 28, 2026 at 11:59 PM Eastern. Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. For position-related questions on your application, contact the search committee chair, Dean Tara Williams ( Tara.Williams@asu.edu ). Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.  ASU’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may