    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189283": {
      "title": "Apply",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Vice President of Research Arizona State University: Knowledge Enterprise Location Tempe campus Open Date Jul 10, 2026 Description Knowledge Enterprise on the Tempe Campus of Arizona State University (ASU) invites applications for the position of Vice President of Research with a concurrent appointment as tenured Professor. The Vice President of Research (VPR) will report to the Executive Vice President (EVP) of Knowledge Enterprise and serves as a member of the core leadership team for the EVP, providing strategic leadership for ASU’s research enterprise, advancing the university’s research mission and accelerating the growth, impact, and national prominence of its research portfolio. The Arizona State University’s Knowledge Enterprise (KE) is a fast-growing research and innovation ecosystem that drives ASU’s research portfolio. Building upon a trajectory that has nearly tripled annual research expenditures over the past decade to more than $1 billion, the VPR will drive initiatives that expand research capacity, strengthen faculty success, and enhance ASU’s competitiveness for external funding and strategic partnerships. The successful candidate will be a distinguished research leader with a record of scholarly achievement and significant experience leading complex research organizations. The ideal candidate will possess deep knowledge of the evolving research landscape, including federal funding priorities, research administration, compliance, technology commercialization, and public-private partnerships. Experience working across disciplines and managing large teams, particularly in science, engineering, health, and emerging technologies, is highly desirable. This leader must exhibit the highest integrity and excellent communication skills, as well as exemplify ASU’s inclusive values and commitment to excellence, fostering an environment of innovation, collaboration, and operational effectiveness aligned with the university’s charter and goals. Essential Functions: Research Strategy, Growth & Portfolio Development Develop and execute a comprehensive strategy to maximize the research productivity and competitiveness of ASU faculty, schools, colleges, institutes, and centers, ensuring the continued growth and impact of the university’s research enterprise. Lead efforts to expand sponsored research activity by identifying and advancing opportunities for federal, state, industry, foundation, and large-scale strategic funding in partnership with academic and research leaders across the university. Assess institutional research strengths, capabilities, and infrastructure to identify areas of competitive advantage and advise senior leadership on opportunities for growth and investment. Partner with institute and initiative leaders to strengthen research capacity, advance strategic project acquisition, and position ASU for transformative research initiatives. Assist with the development and implementation of strategic investment approaches that accelerate growth in priority research areas, monitor outcomes, and ensure alignment with institutional goals. Research Administration, Operations & Service Excellence Oversee research initiatives, and manage administrative support units as assigned, ensuring operational excellence, strategic alignment, and effective stewardship of resources. Ensure the delivery of high-quality research support services across the research lifecycle, including proposal development, pre-award administration, post-award management, and faculty support functions. Provide leadership for research administration, including the development and oversight of research policies, procedures, and operational frameworks that support a world-class research environment. Work with university leadership and stakeholders to align research infrastructure and resource allocation decisions with strategic research priorities and institutional goals. Research Integrity, Compliance & Stewardship Serve as ASU’s Research Integrity Officer, ensuring the highest standards of research ethics, compliance, accountability, and responsible conduct of research. Oversee institutional research compliance programs and ensure adherence to federal, state, sponsor, and university requirements. Promote a culture of integrity, transparency, and responsible research practices across the university’s research enterprise. Ensure effective stewardship of research resources and accountability for investments made in support of ASU’s strategic research priorities. Leadership, Collaboration & External Engagement Serve as a liaison between Knowledge Enterprise and the Academic Enterprise to align faculty recruitment, leadership appointments, and research investments with institutional priorities and emerging opportunities. Collaborate with the Vice President of Innovation, Skysong Innovations, the ASU Foundation, and other university stakeholders to advance ASU’s research, innovation, and commercialization objectives. Work closely with Government Affairs and external relations teams to strengthen ASU’s engagement with federal agencies, policymakers, and research stakeholders, maximizing opportunities to advance faculty research priorities and institutional objectives. Represent ASU and Knowledge Enterprise to external constituencies, including government agencies, industry partners, academic institutions, healthcare organizations, international collaborators, foundations, and community stakeholders. Foster and advance collaborative research initiatives with peer institutions, national laboratories, and strategic partners, including statewide and regional collaborations. Serve as a member of the Knowledge Enterprise Leadership Team and represent the Executive Vice President and Knowledge Enterprise leadership in internal and external engagements as required. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: PhD or similar terminal degree, achievement in research and scholarship to meet the requirements for obtaining tenure and appointment as a full professor. Eight (8) years previous experience in a senior management role with responsibility for development and execution of strategic operational initiatives. A strong record of scholarly or professional achievement and experience managing large teams or complex projects.  Or any equivalent combination of experience and/or education from which comparable knowledge, skills, and abilities have been achieved. Desired Qualifications: Demonstrated expertise in multiple basic or applied sciences with a broad level of knowledge across multiple disciplines. Demonstrated ability to manage and build teams. Experience in working across academic units to achieve research outcomes. Familiarity working with varied funders including federal philanthropic, international, and corporate. Knowledge of business development practices and financial principles in research. Experience with research compliance and regulation. Strong interpersonal skills. Administrative leadership managing faculty and staff. Skill in development and delivery of presentations and public speaking engagements. Application Instructions Only electronic submissions will be reviewed. Incomplete applications will not be considered. To apply for this position, submit the following required application materials electronically to https://apply.interfolio.com/189283 : A detailed cover letter that includes a description of the applicant's administrative experience, research and teaching interests. (limited to 4 pages); A current Curriculum Vitae; and Complete contact information for three professional references (include name, title, affiliation, e-mail address, phone number) in one document. Note: references will only be checked for finalists and in coordination with those candidates. Review of applications will begin August 14, 2026, and, if not filled, subsequent reviews will occur on a rolling basis until the search is closed. For questions, please email Knowledge Enterprise Chief of Staff, Nicole Woodrick at Nicole.Woodrick@asu.edu and include \"Vice President of Research, Knowledge Enterprise\" in the subject line. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.  ASU’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List‎ Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List‎ Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List‎ Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"
