    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190859": {
      "title": "Apply",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Postdoctoral Research Scholar Arizona State University: Knowledge Enterprise: Biodesign Institute: Biodesign Center for Fundamental and Applied Microbiomics Location Tempe Campus Open Date Aug 07, 2026 Description The D’Souza Lab at Arizona State University seeks a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Scholar to join an interdisciplinary research program focused on microbial ecology, molecular biology, bacterial interactions, and the spatial organization of microbial communities. The lab studies how bacteria compete, cooperate, and evolve in structured environments, with a particular emphasis on Type VI secretion system-mediated antagonism, Vibrio ecology, microfluidics, quantitative microscopy, mutant construction, and single-cell analysis. The successful candidate will develop and lead research projects investigating how bacterial interactions shape community structure, growth dynamics, ecological outcomes, and evolutionary trajectories. The position will involve a combination of molecular biology, bacterial genetics, wet-lab microbiology, experimental design, microscopy-based assays, image and data analysis, manuscript preparation, and collaboration with lab members and external collaborators. The appointment will provide opportunities for scientific independence, professional development, fellowship and grant writing, manuscript preparation, conference presentations, and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students. The position is well suited for a researcher interested in combining molecular genetics, microbial ecology, quantitative imaging, and experimental approaches to understand how microbes interact in complex and spatially structured environments. Essential Duties: Design and conduct experiments on microbial interactions, bacterial competition, community ecology, and microbial evolution. Perform molecular biology and bacterial genetics techniques, including: Mutant construction and validation Gene deletions and knockouts Fluorescent reporter and complemented strain development Carry out molecular biology workflows: PCR, cloning, plasmid construction Gibson/HiFi assembly Bacterial transformation and conjugation Colony screening, sequencing verification, and strain archiving Culture and manipulate Vibrio and other bacterial species using standard microbiological techniques. Design and perform: Bacterial competition and growth assays Fluorescence reporter assays Mutant phenotyping experiments Microscopy-based assays to study bacterial interactions Conduct microfluidic experiments and time-lapse fluorescence microscopy to analyze single-cell and community behavior. Analyze microscopy, growth, competition, and other quantitative datasets. Maintain accurate laboratory records, including protocols, strains, plasmids, freezer stocks, and datasets. Contribute to manuscripts, figures, presentations, fellowship applications, and grant reports. Present research findings at lab meetings, seminars, and scientific conferences. Collaborate with research team members and external partners. Mentor graduate and undergraduate students and research staff. Support lab operations, including organization, safety, equipment maintenance, and protocol development. Qualifications Minimum Qualification: PhD in microbiology, molecular biology, bioengineering, or a related field obtained within the last 2 years or less Desired Qualifications: Demonstrated strong background in microbiology, molecular biology, and bacterial genetics. Demonstrated experience with bacterial strain engineering and molecular cloning. Demonstrated familiarity with fluorescence microscopy and microbial assays. Demonstrated experience with quantitative data analysis; programming skills (Python, R, or MATLAB) are a plus. Demonstrated strong communication, organization, and problem-solving skills. Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively. Demonstrated interest in mentoring students and contributing to a positive research environment. Application Instructions Only electronic submissions will be reviewed. Incomplete applications will not be considered. To apply for this position, submit the following required application materials: • Cover letter • A complete curriculum vitae • The names and contact information of three references (name, position, title, organization, email, and phone number). The initial application deadline is Monday August 24, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.  ASU’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List‎ Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are