    "https://apply.interfolio.com/165906": {
      "title": "Associate Dean of Academic & Student Affairs",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Associate Dean of Academic & Student Affairs Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost Location Los Angeles, California Open Date Apr 11, 2025 Description Salary Range $150,000 - $175,000 per year; Offer Dependent on Experience Reporting to the CEO, the Associate Dean of Academic & Student Affairs provides leadership to all academic and student services areas and reflects the mission, vision, and charter of the institution. The Associate Dean of Academic & Student Affairs oversees instructional departments, advising, learning resources, financial aid, recruitment, admissions, and other units assigned by the CCASU CEO. The Associate Dean of Academic & Student Affairs is responsible for student learning, student success, quality of instruction, data-informed decision making, and the pursuit of academic excellence and integrity at CCASU. The Associate Dean of Academic & Student Affairs is an advocate for all academic programs and student services, providing leadership to faculty and staff to ensure consistent quality standards in curriculum and programs that meet the needs of students. The Associate Dean of Academic & Student Affairs provides leadership in long-range planning, budgeting; curriculum; and program development/assessment. The Associate Dean of Academic & Student Affairs ensures compliance with various accreditation agencies as well as state accreditation and regulations. The Associate Dean of Academic & Student Affairs serves on the CCASU executive team. Additionally, the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs maintains relationships with external entities and provides leadership in the areas of retention and graduation of students, and the resources they require to participate in the programs. This full-time position carries the faculty rank of Clinical Professor. The earliest anticipated start date for this position is May 19, 2025. Qualifications Key Responsibilities Provides leadership for planning, developing, and improving instructional programs, which may include but are not limited to liberal arts and workforce programs, faculty initiatives and professional development, academic support, assessment, accreditation compliance, alternate delivery methods, and institutional effectiveness. Fosters intellectual growth, student learning, and scholarly and creative activities by providing academic strategic planning, administrative leadership, direction, and evaluation for all academic activities, faculty affairs, and student services activities at CCASU, providing leadership in fostering campus growth and advancing multidisciplinary programming and scholarship. Leads the ongoing development of the instructional division toward challenging the status quo to elevate the instructional experience to ensure that all students receive the connection, engagement, teaching innovation, and immersive support needed to thrive to achieve their academic and career goals. Provides leadership for the operational planning, management and continuous improvement of student services units, to include advising, financial aid, recruitment, admissions, and learning resources. Demonstrates sound fiscal management and decision-making by overseeing program development, budgets, and facilities of all academic and student affairs units. Coordinates with CCASU Administration and Staff for Enrollment Management in the preparation of the class schedule each semester and approves the final class schedule. Collaborate with the executive team and CCASU Administration and Staff to publish the academic catalog Provides leadership in the recruitment, hiring, orientation, evaluation, retention and professional development of faculty, administration, and staff. Champions faculty development and empowers faculty to become exceptional educators, fostering a learning environment that inspires and motivates students, supporting our journey toward advancing a creative economy. Provides overall direction and leadership to staff assigned to student affairs functions, programs, operations and activities. Leads close collaboration between campus and affiliate units in pursuit of CCASU goals. Works with CCASU & ASU key personnel to establish college-wide protocols for faculty hiring, workload, and other relevant issues. Provides leadership and oversight of curriculum development and implementation of curricula, courses, programs, and activities. Ensures that faculty, academic and student services programs remain compliant with all applicable internal and external rules, regulations, guidelines, and requirements as well as with CCASU policies and procedures. Manages, monitors, and administers area budgets. Implements budget controls and perform needs assessments for development of annual budgeting recommendations. Reviews, analyzes, and evaluates instructional programs for continuous improvement. Make recommendations to the CCASU CEO about the creation, improvement, and deactivation of instructional programs in collaboration with the college’s academic community. Resolves student, faculty, and dean's issues/grievances and academic appeals through collaboration and appropriate appeal processes. Develops and pursues professional relationships with area K-12 school systems, higher education institutions, and community organizations to increase educational partnerships and to determine community educational needs within the college's service area. Participate as a college representative on various committees, meetings, and conferences. Promotes an environment supportive of the CCASU mission, vision, charter, and strategic plan. Provides effective, creative, and energetic leadership by promoting, supporting, and evaluating innovative approaches to teaching and learning and student success. Responsible for other reasonable related duties as assigned. Preferred Skills Understanding of the unique challenges and opportunities in higher education. Experience with assessment, accreditation processes and regulatory compliance. Strong interpersonal and conflict-resolution abilities. A collaborative leadership style that inspires and empowers others. Qualifications Doctorate or master’s degree in education administration, curriculum development, educational leadership, or a specific academic discipline. Teaching Experience: At least 5-7 years of experience as a faculty member or educator in K-12 or higher education settings. Administrative Leadership: 5-10+ years in leadership positions, such as Dean, Department Chair, Provost, or Director. Proven experience overseeing academic programs, curriculum development, faculty management, program assessment and strategic initiatives. Proven ability to advance comprehensive excellence in academic and student services settings. Exceptional communication, strategic planning, and decision-making skills. Work Environment This is a key leadership role that requires a presence on campus, with occasional travel to represent CCASU at external events. The Associate Dean of Academic & Student Affairs plays a pivotal role in shaping the academic future of the institution and ensuring its ongoing success. Location This is an in-person position that this housed at the California College of ASU in Los Angeles, California. Application Instructions The application deadline is May 15, 2025 (30 days after the position is posted nationally). Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. Candidates will be asked to create or use an existing Interfolio Dossier to submit the following application materials: Cover Letter Current Curriculum Vita (CV) Personal Statement Contact information for three professional references; phone and email Questions about the position should be directed to Rena Wright, California College of ASU, Director of Human Resources at rwrigh45@californiacollege.asu.edu Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.  ASU’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List‎ Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List‎ Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List‎ Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"
